  "summary": "Partial reversal of image tones caused by exposing developed silver halide to light during development.",
  "description": "Creates distinctive dark lines around highlights and a partial inversion of tones, producing a ghostly, silhouette-like effect. Named after French photographer Sabattier who documented it systematically in the 19th century, though the effect was discovered accidentally earlier.",
  "culturalContext": "Initially, the term \"solarization\" was used to describe the effect observed in cases of extreme overexposure of the photographic film or plate in the camera.",
